    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual</a></i> </p><p><i>See also:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Techniques\" title=\"Force Techniques\">Force Techniques</a></i> </p><p>You can spend a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Force Point\">Force Point</a> to cause your <i><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Light\" title=\"Force Light\">Force Light</a></i> to blind those it harms; any creature that takes damage from <i><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Light\" title=\"Force Light\">Force Light</a></i> grants <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Concealment\" title=\"Concealment\">Concealment</a> to all other targets until the end of it's next turn. You can spend a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Destiny_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Destiny Point\">Destiny Point</a> to change this to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Total_Concealment\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Total Concealment\">Total Concealment</a> instead. </p>",
